<title>INDIA: Indian minister proposes raising edible oil duty.</title>
<headline>Indian minister proposes raising edible oil duty.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian Agriculture Minister Chaturanan Mishra said on Wednesday that he has written to Finance Minister P. Chidambaram proposing that the import duty on edible oils be increased to 30 percent from 20 percent.  </p>
<p>Mishra told a news conference after a meeting with state agriculture ministers in the Indian capital that he had received complaints from industry officials that edible oil imports were cheaper than domestic production.</p>
<p>&quot;I have written to the finance miniter to increase the edible oil import duty from 20 percent to 30 percent,&quot; Mishra said.</p>
<p>He did not indicate whether Chidambaram had replied to his request.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
